{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.exists_cs_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.exists_cs_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L225-L243","doc":"**Vanishing Chern–Simons point (derived, falsifiable).**  Granting both\nclasses, the Stokes constant being nonzero (`A_ω ≠ 0`), and the two\nmeasured anchor signs, the IVT zero crossing is a substrate point where\n`A_ω · Im 𝔙(u(q*)) = 0`, i.e. (for `A_ω ≠ 0`) the deformed complex\nvolume is purely REAL — the Chern–Simons part vanishes:\n`Im 𝔙(u(q*)) = 0`.  A geometric prediction of the composed\nconjectures. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.phiB_eq_cs_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.phiB_eq_cs_phase","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L215-L223","doc":"**The `Φ_b` readout is the Stokes-scaled Chern–Simons phase (derived).**\nComposing the unimodular readout with the channel identity: at the\nidentified argument, `Φ_b = e^{i · A_ω · CS(u(q₀))}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.phase_eq_im_deformed_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.phase_eq_im_deformed_volume","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L203-L213","doc":"**Two-conjecture composition (derived).**  Under the keystone argument\nidentification AND the S_K-channel of the complex-volume conjecture, the\nfibre-branch `Φ_b` phase at the identified argument equals the\nStokes-scaled deformed Chern–Simons part — the precise form of \"`Φ_b`\ntouches binding ONLY through the `conj:binding-qbeta-complex-volume`\nchannel\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.S_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.S_eq","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L201-L201","doc":"The channel identity `S_K(q₀) = A_ω · Im 𝔙(u(q₀))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.A_ω","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.A_ω","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L199-L199","doc":"The GGM Stokes constant (= 3 for 4₁). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.V","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L197-L197","doc":"The deformed complex volume `𝔙(u) = Vol(u) + i·CS(u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.u","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L195-L195","doc":"The substrate → deformation map `u(q₀)` (log meridian holonomy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L193-L193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SDeformedVolumeChannel","kind":"class","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L176-L201","doc":"**The S_K-channel of the complex-volume conjecture (§3b class).**  Carries\nthe three open inputs of the binding side of\n`conj:binding-qbeta-complex-volume` for the S_K observable:\n\n* `u` — the substrate → deformation map (log meridian holonomy), the\n  open map every S-route converges on. `u(q₀) = ln q₀ + i·ϑ_K(q₀)`,\n  where `ϑ_K` is the knot-dependent angular deformation (bean `qou-qnnq`);\n* `V` — the deformed complex volume `𝔙(u) = Vol(u) + i·CS(u)` (a\n  theorem for `4₁`, explicitly computable via Neumann–Zagier);\n* `A_ω` — the GGM Stokes constant (= 3 for 4₁; discrete integer,\n  DT/BPS invariant; needs Faddeev rigidity — beans `qou-rp5f`, `qou-cons`);\n* `S_eq` — the channel identity: the S_K-leak is the Stokes-scaled\n  imaginary (Chern–Simons) part at the deformed point.\n\nThe class asserts nothing provable-outright; instances are the open\nconjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.exists_pure_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.exists_pure_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L134-L151","doc":"**Pure bar-even point (derived from the class).**  Under the keystone\nidentification, the zero crossing is a substrate point where the Φ_b\nphase at the identified argument vanishes exactly and the Φ_b value is\n`1` — the bar-odd leak switches off and `c₃ = −Vol(4₁)` is purely\nbar-even there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.exists_zero_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.exists_zero_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L118-L132","doc":"**Intermediate-value zero crossing (unconditional).**  If `S` is\ncontinuous on `q₀ > 1` and takes a positive value at one anchor and a\nnegative value at a later one, it vanishes somewhere between.  This is\nthe audited sign-flip observation: `S(muon) > 0 > S(proton)` forces a\nsubstrate `q*` between the anchors with `S(q*) = 0` — i.e.\n`c₃ = −Vol(4₁)` exactly, purely bar-even.  (The two measured signs\nenter as hypotheses: measured values are not Lean-provable.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.readout_phiB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.readout_phiB","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L107-L116","doc":"**Unimodular readout form (derived).**  Under the identification, the\nΦ_b value at the identified argument is the pure phase `e^{iS(q₀)}` —\nthe S-leak is literally the argument of a σ-unitary, matching the\nbar-odd phase reframe `𝔔_β/Q_A = cos Φ(u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification.readout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification.readout","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L105-L105","doc":"The Φ_b phase at the identified argument reproduces the S-leak. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification.S_continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification.S_continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L103-L103","doc":"Continuity of the S-map on the physical domain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.SArgumentIdentification","kind":"class","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L84-L105","doc":"**The keystone conjecture (§3b primary class).**  The given argument map\n`zArg` realizes the S-leak through the fibre-branch `Φ_b` phase:\n\n* `S_continuousOn` — the S-map varies continuously on the physical\n  domain `q₀ > 1` (the hypothesis under which the measured sign flip\n  `S(muon) > 0 > S(proton)` forces a zero crossing);\n* `readout` — at every substrate modulus the Faddeev phase at the\n  identified argument IS the S-leak: `phase (b(q₀)) (zArg q₀) = S q₀`.\n\nThe intended `zArg` is the substrate → meridian-holonomy map of the\npole↔cusp matching (`conj:algebraic-geometric-dilog-equivalence`); the\nclass is parametrized by the map precisely so that it carries that\nstructural content rather than a vacuous pointwise choice (module\ndocstring).  An instance for the structural map is the OPEN state —\nnone is fabricated here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreQParam_fibreB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreQParam_fibreB","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L71-L82","doc":"**The fibre modular parameter at the substrate is the pure phase\n`e^{i·ln q₀ / 2}`** — `|q_b| = 1` with the substrate modulus as the\nangle.  (Contrast the product branch, where `q_b = e^{-t} = 1/q₀` is\nreal inside the disc.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreB_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreB_sq","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L66-L69","doc":"`b(q₀)² = ln q₀ / 2π` on `q₀ ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreB_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreB_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L62-L64","doc":"The fibre b-map is positive on the physical domain `q₀ > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification.fibreB","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBSArgumentIdentification.lean#L53-L60","doc":"The **fibre b-map** `b(q₀) = √(ln q₀ / 2π)`: the real-`b` (fibre-branch)\ncounterpart of the product-branch substrate map\n`√(ln q₀/2π)·e^{iπ/4}` (`QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd.substrateB`) — the\n`e^{iπ/4}` phase removed, so the modular parameter lands ON the unit\ncircle instead of inside it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}